<style type="text/css">@font-face {font-family:'Space Mono';font-style:normal;font-weight:700;src:url(/cf-fonts/s/space-mono/5.2.9/latin-ext/700/normal.woff2);unicode-range:U+0100-02BA,U+02BD-02C5,U+02C7-02CC,U+02CE-02D7,U+02DD-02FF,U+0304,U+0308,U+0329,U+1D00-1DBF,U+1E00-1E9F,U+1EF2-1EFF,U+2020,U+20A0-20AB,U+20AD-20C0,U+2113,U+2C60-2C7F,U+A720-A7FF;font-display:swap;}@font-face {font-family:'Space Mono';font-style:normal;font-weight:700;src:url(/cf-fonts/s/space-mono/5.2.9/latin/700/normal.woff2);unicode-range:U+0000-00FF,U+0131,U+0152-0153,U+02BB-02BC,U+02C6,U+02DA,U+02DC,U+0304,U+0308,U+0329,U+2000-206F,U+20AC,U+2122,U+2191,U+2193,U+2212,U+2215,U+FEFF,U+FFFD;font-display:swap;}@font-face {font-family:'Space Mono';font-style:normal;font-weight:700;src:url(/cf-fonts/s/space-mono/5.2.9/vietnamese/700/normal.woff2);unicode-range:U+0102-0103,U+0110-0111,U+0128-0129,U+0168-0169,U+01A0-01A1,U+01AF-01B0,U+0300-0301,U+0303-0304,U+0308-0309,U+0323,U+0329,U+1EA0-1EF9,U+20AB;font-display:swap;}</style>

<!-- Structured data. This is what a search engine or an agent reads to learn
     that the accounts below are the same organisation as this domain.

     This list is deliberately NOT a copy of the registry in
     docs/DOMAINS_AND_SOCIALS.md — some live accounts are held back from this
     domain on purpose. An account being live is not a reason to add it here.
     Read README.md §"Crawlers and agents" before touching this array.

     `application/ld+json` is a DATA BLOCK, not an executed script, so the CSP's
     `script-src` (which has no 'self' and no 'unsafe-inline') does not apply.
     Verified in-browser against the exact `_headers` policy: no
     securitypolicyviolation, element present in the DOM. Do not "fix" this by
     adding 'self' to script-src.

     No email field on purpose. Cloudflare's Email Address Obfuscation rewrites
     addresses it finds in the HTML, and inside a JSON block that would produce
     invalid JSON. The page carries no contact address at all now; if one is
     ever added to the body it needs the email_off markers — see README.md
     §"The contact address". -->
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Organization",
  "name": "FLOP",
  "url": "https://flop.finance/",
  "logo": "https://flop.finance/assets/flop-lockup-reverse.svg",
  "description": "$FLOP is food for your AI agent.",
  "sameAs": [
    "https://x.com/flop_labs",
    "https://www.youtube.com/@flop_labs",
    "https://www.tiktok.com/@flop_labs",
    "https://github.com/flop-labs"
  ]
}
</script>

<style>
  /* Palette values are the specified hex from Logo & Usage Standards V1.0 §4,
     which is also DESIGN.md's canonical palette. The lockup SVG is the approved
     master unaltered, so its own Ice White sits ~3/255 off this ground's spec
     Ice White — imperceptible, and the two never touch. See
     docs/brand/official/README.md. */
  :root {
    --base: #0A1128;       /* the ground */
    --ice-white: #F5F7FA;  /* the word mark, and the tagline */
    --accent: #00B4D8;     /* the Chip, and the links — nothing else */
  }

  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

  html, body { height: 100%; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--base);
    color: var(--ice-white);
    font-family: 'Space Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
  }

  main {
    min-height: 100svh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    /* Page margin sits outside the logo's own clear space, never inside it.
       The `svh` terms only ever *reduce* the width-derived value, so a short
       viewport tightens the stack and a tall one is left exactly as it was. */
    padding: clamp(24px, min(6vw, 5svh), 64px);
    gap: clamp(32px, min(7vw, 7svh), 72px);
  }

  /* The delivered SVG already carries the mandated 4X clear space inside its
     own canvas (measured: cap height 8 modules => X; padding = 4X on the long
     edges, more on the short). So the <img> box IS artwork + 4X, and the flex
     `gap` above is headroom on top of the minimum — never a substitute for it.

     Minimum-size floor: the artwork spans 81.6% of the file width, so the
     One-color threshold of 200px artwork needs ~245px of file width. At the
     320px viewport floor, 78vw = 250px file => 204px of artwork. The two-tone
     lockup therefore stays legal at every viewport, and the hard 120px
     logotype minimum is never approached.

     The `62svh` term keeps the whole stack inside a short desktop viewport —
     without it the apply line falls below a fold this page gives no cue to
     scroll past. `max(..., 250px)` is what keeps the height term from ever
     breaching the floor above: on a landscape phone (844x390) 62svh would be
     242px of file => 197px of artwork, under the 200px threshold at which V1.0
     requires the One-color version. Clamped at 250px it stays at 204px of
     artwork and the page simply scrolls instead. Brand floor beats fold.
     If you retune any of these numbers, redo this arithmetic. */
  .lockup {
    display: block;
    width: min(78vw, max(62svh, 250px), 620px);
    height: auto;
  }

  /* The tagline is page copy, not part of the lockup: the standard forbids
     locking a tagline to the logo. It is kept visually independent and well
     outside the clear space. */
  .tagline {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 34ch;
    font-size: clamp(19px, 4.4vw, 34px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* Launch facts + contact. Page copy like the tagline: same voice, one step
     down in scale so the tagline stays the loudest line under the lockup. */
  .points {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 46ch;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(14px, min(3vw, 2.6svh), 22px);
    font-size: clamp(14px, 2.6vw, 19px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.45;
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .points p { margin: 0; }

  /* The Chip carries the colour — but a link has to read as a link, so the
     accent is spent on links (including the social row) and nowhere else. */
  .points a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* Each item on the apply line is atomic. Without this the line breaks inside
     a label — "GPU / providers (miners)" — because the interpuncts are not the
     only break opportunities the browser sees. Wrapping is still allowed, but
     only at the separators. */
  .apply a { white-space: nowrap; }

  /* The classic follow row. Icons are links, so they take the accent like any
     other link; no underline, because there is no text to underline. The tap
     target is padded out to ~44px per platform guidance while the glyph itself
     stays at 22px. */
  .social {
    display: flex;
    gap: clamp(6px, 2vw, 14px);
  }

  .social a {
    display: flex;
    padding: 11px;
    color: var(--accent);
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .social svg {
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    fill: currentColor;
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .social a:hover { color: var(--ice-white); }
  }

  .social a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* Language switcher. <details> because this page's CSP has no 'self' and no
     'unsafe-inline' in script-src — the landing pages' JS dropdown and their
     flop_lang cookie are both impossible here, so the picker has to be plain
     HTML. A <details> disclosure is exactly that: keyboard accessible, no JS,
     and it degrades to an always-open list if CSS fails. The consequence is
     that a visitor's choice is NOT remembered between visits; hreflang is what
     points search engines at the right one. */
  .lang {
    font-size: clamp(12px, 2.2vw, 14px);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .lang summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 6px 10px;
  }

  .lang summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }

  .lang summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .lang ul {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 4px 14px;
    max-width: 44ch;
  }

  .lang a {
    color: var(--ice-white);
    text-decoration: none;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .lang a[aria-current="true"] { color: var(--accent); opacity: 1; }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .lang a:hover { opacity: 1; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    main > * { animation: rise 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1) both; }
    main > :nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 0.12s; }
    main > :nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 0.24s; }
    /* The social row is main's 4th child. Without its own delay it animates in
       lockstep with the lockup and the stagger visibly breaks. */
    main > :nth-child(4) { animation-delay: 0.36s; }
    /* The language switcher is the 5th child. */
    main > :nth-child(5) { animation-delay: 0.48s; }
    @keyframes rise {
      from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); }
      to   { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <!-- Approved master, byte-for-byte. Never recolour, crop, rotate, or re-export
         it, and never apply a CSS filter to it. Reverse lockup is approved on
         Base only. -->
    <img
      class="lockup"
      src="/assets/flop-lockup-reverse.svg"
      alt="FLOP"
      width="2000"
      height="1000"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
    <!-- lang/dir are load-bearing, not decoration: the tagline stays English in
         every locale, and inside an RTL page bidi otherwise moves the leading "$"
         and the trailing "." to the wrong ends — observed as "FLOP is food for$"
         on /ar/. Same reason the @handle below is marked. -->
    <p class="tagline" lang="en" dir="ltr">$FLOP is food for your AI&nbsp;agent.</p>
    <div class="points">
      <p>No pre-sale</p>
      <p>No VCs</p>
      <p>100% fair launch</p>
      <p>Follow <a href="https://x.com/flop_labs" rel="me noopener" dir="ltr">@flop_labs</a> for airdrop eligibility</p>
      <!-- Applications. These are OUR URLs; `_redirects` maps them to the
           Google Forms and is the only place those form ids live. Never paste
           a docs.google.com URL back in here — the indirection is what lets a
           re-created form be fixed in one line without breaking every link
           already loose in the world. deploy.sh verifies the targets still
           answer as FLOP forms before it will publish.

           A redirect to Google is a plain outbound navigation, so the CSP in
           `_headers` needs nothing: `form-action 'none'` governs submissions
           made FROM this page, and there is no live `navigate-to` directive.
           Only ever embedding a form in an <iframe> would need `frame-src`.

           All three forms now exist, so all three are links. -->
      <p class="apply">Apply —
        <a href="/apply/miner" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GPU providers (miners)</a> ·
        <a href="/apply/validator" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Validators</a> ·
        <a href="/apply/kol" target="_blank" rel="noopener">KOLs & creators</a>
      </p>
      <!-- The teaser. Deliberately NOT a template placeholder: render() raises on a key
           missing from any catalog, so a placeholder means eleven translations of a
           label that points at an English-only document. It is marked lang/dir for the
           same bidi reason as the tagline and the @handle — inside /ar/ an unmarked
           English string has its leading and trailing characters reordered. Same
           treatment, same reason, documented in gen_flop_finance.py. -->
      <p class="teaser" lang="en" dir="ltr"><a href="/teaser/">Read the teaser →</a></p>
    </div>
    <!-- This row is X only, and which accounts may appear on this domain at all
         is decided in README.md §"Crawlers and agents" — not by what is marked
         live in docs/DOMAINS_AND_SOCIALS.md. Never link a handle that is still
         "Claim" in that table either: it invites someone else to squat it.

         Icons are inline SVG because `img-src 'self'` forbids an icon CDN, and
         because an <img> cannot inherit the accent. Paths are the standard
         simple-icons glyphs on a 24×24 grid. -->
    <nav class="social" aria-label="FLOP on social media">
      <a href="https://x.com/flop_labs" rel="me noopener" aria-label="FLOP on X">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M18.901 1.153h3.68l-8.04 9.19L24 22.846h-7.406l-5.8-7.584-6.638 7.584H.474l8.6-9.83L0 1.154h7.594l5.243 6.932ZM17.61 20.644h2.039L6.486 3.24H4.298Z"/></svg>
      </a>
    </nav>
    <details class="lang">
      <summary>Language · English</summary>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/?lang=en" hreflang="en" lang="en" aria-current="true">English</a></li>
        <li><a href="/zh/" hreflang="zh" lang="zh">中文</a></li>
        <li><a href="/ja/" hreflang="ja" lang="ja">日本語</a></li>
        <li><a href="/ko/" hreflang="ko" lang="ko">한국어</a></li>
        <li><a href="/ru/" hreflang="ru" lang="ru">Русский</a></li>
        <li><a href="/ar/" hreflang="ar" lang="ar">العربية</a></li>
        <li><a href="/pt-BR/" hreflang="pt-BR" lang="pt-BR">Português (Brasil)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/es/" hreflang="es" lang="es">Español</a></li>
        <li><a href="/fr/" hreflang="fr" lang="fr">Français</a></li>
        <li><a href="/de/" hreflang="de" lang="de">Deutsch</a></li>
        <li><a href="/tr/" hreflang="tr" lang="tr">Türkçe</a></li>
      </ul>
    </details>
  </main>
